nodecode-channel-whatsapp-agent is a rewrite of ahtishamdilawar's
ahtishamdilawar/hermes-whatsapp-agent-platform:

  https://github.com/ahtishamdilawar/hermes-whatsapp-agent-platform
  commit 3a57b1da04499279d1af6c7d979c9c2d8b658ce0

MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Ahtisham Dilawar (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the whole channel, in Common Lisp, against Nodecode's channel
kit. The Python platform adapter, its long-poll loop, the update-to-event
mapping, the send/status/media calls and the config section became a
Nodecode room cell: the same `GET /agent/v1/updates` long poll, the same
`POST /agent/v1/messages` text send with a quoted context, the same
`POST /agent/v1/statuses` read receipt carrying the typing indicator, and
the same rule that only the agent's creator may drive it, with the same
fail-closed section instead of Hermes's own config and session plumbing. A
file is carried the way the original carries it: inbound media is fetched
through `GET /media/{id}` with the key and handed on as an attachment, and
an answer's file is uploaded with `POST /media` (form-data) and posted as
the message of its kind, under the same `media_enabled` switch. The
words leave as the original leaves them: its formatting.py markdown-to-
WhatsApp conversion (`**bold**` to *bold*, `*it*` to _it_, `~~s~~` to
~s~, a heading to a bold line, a link to its words and its address, code
untouched) and its CHUNK_LIMIT/MAX_TEXT_LENGTH split, counting UTF-16
units as an emoji is counted, with a caption kept to Meta's 1024 and said
first when it does not fit or the kind takes none.

Left out: `DELETE /media` (the adapter never deleted a file, and neither
does this one), the inbound size/sha256 verification and the download
cache, the media-transcode and re-upload-on-refusal retry, the in-chat
reaction hooks, the richer error taxonomy and rate windows (the cell
relies on the kit's retry and the sender's own pacing), and Hermes's own
JSON state file: the cursor, the lane's first standing and the ids already
answered are kept in Nodecode's store instead, under the same rules.
